Toad URL Cleaner

TypeScript adaptation of Clipboard Cleaner's URL engine and bundled rule data:
https://github.com/thetoadsage/clipboard-cleaner/tree/936a4b357a6693ae7465feec1945bd4acbe25bc6
Original implementation Copyright (c) 2026 thetoadsage, MIT license.
Modifications: JavaScript URL parsing, URL extraction from Discord text, optional
canonical rewrites, and independent copy/send/edit settings. Credential-bearing
and custom-port URLs are not canonicalized. Message code spans are preserved.

Valenced Clear URLs by hakuxyz and nexpid supplies the integration reference:
https://github.com/Valenced/valenced-community-plugins/tree/main/plugins/clear-urls
Its NOTICE attributes send/edit patching to nexpid's RevengePlugins (CC BY 4.0):
https://github.com/nexpid/RevengePlugins/blob/main/src/plugins/clean-urls/src/stuff/patcher.ts
https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/
This adaptation uses property-based discovery and supports object message payloads.

tracking-rules.json retains its ClearURLs/Rules LGPL-3.0 provenance and reviewed
uBlock Origin uAssets GPL-3.0 subset. Upstream commit identifiers are embedded
in that file. Provider exceptions and conditional/preservation rules are retained.
See licenses/ for license texts and the original Clipboard Cleaner MIT notice.

URL parsing uses react-native-url-polyfill 4.0.0, Copyright (c) Nicolas Charpentier,
MIT license (included in licenses/URL-Polyfill-MIT.txt). It is bundled locally;
this plugin does not install global polyfills or fetch URLs/rules at runtime.

